# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[make]] something by merging parts. {{defdate|from later 15th c.}}
#: {{ux|en|The editor '''composed''' a historical journal from many individual letters.}}
#* '''December 22 1678''', {{w|Thomas Sprat}}, ''A Sermon Preached before the King at White-Hall''
#*: Zeal ought to be '''composed''' of the highest degrees of all pious affection.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[make up]] the whole; to [[constitute]].
#: {{ux|en|A church is '''composed''' of its members.}}
#* {{RQ:Watts Improvement
|passage=A few useful things {{...}} '''compose''' their intellectual possessions.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|nonstandard}} To [[comprise]].
# {{lb|en|transitive|or|intransitive}} To [[construct]] by mental labor; to [[think up]]; particularly, to produce or create a [[literary]] or musical work.
#: {{ux|en|The orator '''composed''' his speech over the week prior.}}
#: {{ux|en|Nine numbered symphonies, including the Fifth, were '''composed''' by Beethoven.}}
#: {{ux|en|It's difficult to '''compose''' without absolute silence.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1714|author=w:Alexander Pope|title=Imitation of Horace, Book II. Sat. 6
|passage=Let me {{...}} '''compose''' / Something in Verse as true as Prose.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1838|author=w:Benjamin Haydon|title=Painting, and the fine arts
|passage=the genius that '''composed''' such works as the "Standard" and "Last Supper"}}
# {{lb|en|sometimes|reflexive}} To [[calm]]; to free from agitation.
#: {{ux|en|Try to '''compose''' your thoughts.}}
#: {{ux|en|The defendant couldn't '''compose''' herself and was found in contempt.}}
#* {{RQ:Dryden Aeneis|passage='''Compose''' thy mind; / Nor frauds are here contrived, nor force designed.}}
# To arrange the elements of a [[photograph]] or other picture.
# To [[settle]] (an argument, dispute etc.); to come to a [[settlement]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010|author=w:Christopher Hitchens|title=Hitch-22|publisher=Atlantic|year_published=2011|page=280
|passage=By trying his best to '''compose''' matters with the mullahs, he had sincerely shown that he did not seek a violent collision {{...}}}}
# To [[arrange]] in proper form; to reduce to order; to put in proper state or condition.
#* {{RQ:Dryden Aeneis|passage=In a peaceful grave my corpse '''compose'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=2|passage=How in safety best we may / '''Compose''' our present evils.|year=1873}}
# {{lb|en|printing|dated}} To arrange ([[type]]s) in a [[composing stick]] for printing; to [[typeset]].

