## The [[configuration]] of [[planet]]s at a [[given#Adjective|given]] [[time#Noun|time]] (especially a person's [[birth#Noun|birth]]), as [[believe]]d to [[affect#Verb|affect]] [[event#Noun|events]] on [[Earth]], or used for [[determine|determining]] a [[horoscope]].
##* {{RQ:Elyot Governour|chapter=The Diuision of Ingratitude and the Dispraise therof|pages=188–189|pageref=188|passage=But alas such peruerse '''constellation''' nowe reigneth ouer men, that where some be aptely and naturally disposed to amitie, and fyndeth one, in similitude of studie and maners, equall to his expectation, and therfore kendeleth a feruent loue towarde that persone, puttinge all his ioye and delite in the praise and auauncement of him that he loueth, it hapneth that he which is loued, beinge promoted in honour, either of purpose neglecteth his frende, therby suppressynge libertie of speche or familiar resorte; or els esteming his mynde with his fortune onely, and nat with the suertie of frendship, hideth from him the secretes of his harte, and either trusteth no man, or els him whome prosperous fortune hath late brought in acquaintaunce.}}
##* {{RQ:Eliot Romola|volume=I|chapter=First Impressions|page=72|passage=[H]e was born under the '''constellation''' that gives a man skill, riches, and integrity, whatever that '''constellation''' may be, which is of the less consequence because babies can't choose their own horoscopes, and, indeed, if they could, there might be an inconvenient rush of babies at particular epochs.}}
## A person's [[character#Noun|character]] or [[inclination]]s, [[supposedly]] determined by their horoscope.
##* {{RQ:Shakespeare Twelfth Night|act=I|scene=iv|page=257|column=2|passage=I knovv thy '''conſtellation''' is right apt / For this affayre: {{...}}}}
