# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A [[count]] or [[earl]].
# {{lb|en|obsolete|or|historical}} A [[councillor]], ''[[particularly]]:''
## {{lb|en|historical}} A [[member]] of [[early modern]] [[city council]]s in southern [[France]] and [[Catalonia]].
## {{lb|en|historical}} An [[officer]] of the [[trading]] and [[merchant]] [[companies]] of [[early modern]] [[England]].
## {{lb|en|historical}} An [[official]] in [[various]] [[early modern]] [[port]] and [[trading]] [[town]]s, [[elect]]ed by [[resident]] [[foreign]] [[merchant]]s to [[settle]] [[dispute]]s among themselves and to [[represent]] them to the [[local]] [[authorities]].
# {{lb|en|by extension}} An [[official]] [[residing]] in [[major]] [[foreign]] [[town]]s to [[represent]] and [[protect]] the [[interest]]s of the [[merchant]]s and [[citizen]]s of their [[country]].
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A [[high]] [[government]] [[official]], generally either a [[coruler]] himself or a [[counsellor]] directly under the [[ruler]].
#* {{RQ:Marlowe Tamburlaine|part=1|scene=ii|page=26|passage=Both we will raigne as '''Conſuls''' of the earth,<br />And mightie kings ſhall be our Senators.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Othello|I|II|312|1|And many of the '''Conſuls''', rais'd and met, <br /> Are at the Dukes already.}}
